+{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_orig_mnqwy3c7hazdknbsmizdqm3dge3ginjyga3gcmzwmqytcza","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Phase 4: Delayed/Scheduled Tasks\n2\t\n3\tAdd support for delayed and scheduled task execution.\n4\t\n5\t## Updated Methods\n6\t\n7\t- **`enqueue(queueName, payload, options?)`** - Options can now include:\n8\t  - `delay`: number of milliseconds before the task becomes available\n9\t  - `runAt`: a `Date` object specifying when the task should become available\n10\t  - (existing) `priority`: priority level\n11\t\n12\t## Requirements\n13\t\n14\t- A delayed task is enqueued immediately but not returned by `dequeue()` until the delay has elapsed\n15\t- A `runAt` task becomes available at the specified time\n16\t- Non-delayed tasks should be dequeued before delayed tasks that haven't become available yet\n17\t- When multiple delayed tasks are available, they are ordered by their availability time (earliest first), then by priority, then FIFO\n18\t- `delay` and `runAt` work with named queues\n19\t- The task object should include a `availableAt` property (Date) indicating when the task becomes available\n20\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bb6276d8-e493-46dd-af72-8571635da619","uuid":"2d388759-7e1f-44e2-9c5b-714207112f59","timestamp":"2026-06-18T06:10:49.901Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/workspace/phases/phase-04.md","content":"# Phase 4: Delayed/Scheduled Tasks\n\nAdd support for delayed and scheduled task execution.\n\n## Updated Methods\n\n- **`enqueue(queueName, payload, options?)`** - Options can now include:\n  - `delay`: number of milliseconds before the task becomes available\n  - `runAt`: a `Date` object specifying when the task should become available\n  - (existing) `priority`: priority level\n\n## Requirements\n\n- A delayed task is enqueued immediately but not returned by `dequeue()` until the delay has elapsed\n- A `runAt` task becomes available at the specified time\n- Non-delayed tasks should be dequeued before delayed tasks that haven't become available yet\n- When multiple delayed tasks are available, they are ordered by their availability time (earliest first), then by priority, then FIFO\n- `delay` and `runAt` work with named queues\n- The task object should include a `availableAt` property (Date) indicating when the task becomes available\n","numLines":20,"startLine":1,"totalLines":20}}}
+{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_orig_mnqwy3c7mi2tamtgmu4wkyrxmyydqmtegbsgimddmmydkyy","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Phase 5: Retry with Backoff\n2\t\n3\tAdd automatic retry functionality with exponential backoff.\n4\t\n5\t## New Methods\n6\t\n7\t- **`fail(taskId, error?)`** - Mark a processing task as failed. Triggers automatic retry if retries remain.\n8\t- **`complete(taskId)`** - Mark a processing task as completed.\n9\t\n10\t## Updated Methods\n11\t\n12\t- **`enqueue(queueName, payload, options?)`** - Options can now include:\n13\t  - `maxRetries`: maximum number of retry attempts (default: 3)\n14\t  - `backoffMs`: base delay for exponential backoff in milliseconds (default: 1000)\n15\t\n16\t## Requirements\n17\t\n18\t- When `fail()` is called and retries remain, the task is re-enqueued with a delay\n19\t- Backoff formula: `backoffMs * 2^(attempt - 1)` where attempt starts at 1\n20\t  - 1st retry: 1000ms, 2nd retry: 2000ms, 3rd retry: 4000ms\n21\t- `task.attempts` tracks how many times the task has been attempted (starts at 1 on first dequeue)\n22\t- Custom `maxRetries` can be set per task\n23\t- Retried tasks preserve their original queue name and priority\n24\t- If a task has exhausted all retries, it remains in `failed` status (see Phase 6 for DLQ)\n25\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bb6276d8-e493-46dd-af72-8571635da619","uuid":"99eb286d-bb2f-41f1-8b9d-061f7f5d95d6","timestamp":"2026-06-18T06:10:49.901Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/workspace/phases/phase-05.md","content":"# Phase 5: Retry with Backoff\n\nAdd automatic retry functionality with exponential backoff.\n\n## New Methods\n\n- **`fail(taskId, error?)`** - Mark a processing task as failed. Triggers automatic retry if retries remain.\n- **`complete(taskId)`** - Mark a processing task as completed.\n\n## Updated Methods\n\n- **`enqueue(queueName, payload, options?)`** - Options can now include:\n  - `maxRetries`: maximum number of retry attempts (default: 3)\n  - `backoffMs`: base delay for exponential backoff in milliseconds (default: 1000)\n\n## Requirements\n\n- When `fail()` is called and retries remain, the task is re-enqueued with a delay\n- Backoff formula: `backoffMs * 2^(attempt - 1)` where attempt starts at 1\n  - 1st retry: 1000ms, 2nd retry: 2000ms, 3rd retry: 4000ms\n- `task.attempts` tracks how many times the task has been attempted (starts at 1 on first dequeue)\n- Custom `maxRetries` can be set per task\n- Retried tasks preserve their original queue name and priority\n- If a task has exhausted all retries, it remains in `failed` status (see Phase 6 for DLQ)\n","numLines":25,"startLine":1,"totalLines":25}}}
